{
  "supported": true,
  "coverage": "partial",
  "coverage_explanation": "Exercises initial readings, humidity-only changes, temperature-only changes, simultaneous changes, a negative temperature, and returns to previously displayed values. Checks both numeric fields, their required labels and positions, display initialization, landscape rotation, white text, size 2, black background, and LCD control-pin configuration. Also checks the public setup deadline. DHT updates are allowed the cached sensor acquisition interval and the public fresh-reading allowance rather than incorrectly demanding an uncached reading within 250ms. The suite does not independently prove the exact 100ms delay at the end of every loop, source-level object/library declarations, or that a black clear operation occurs on every change; background metadata verifies configuration rather than the complete graphics operation history.",
  "assumptions": [
    "The supplied wiring is preserved: hardware SPI uses MOSI 11, MISO 12 and SCK 13; LCD CS is 10, D/C is 9 and RST is 8; DHT22 data is pin 2. No unspecified LED, button or analog bench defaults are needed.",
    "Each sensor state persists for 4000ms, exceeding the disclosed DHT API's 2s caching interval. Changed-reading windows allow up to 3250ms for sensor freshness and subsequent display response.",
    "Numeric formatting may use different decimal precision, but the explicitly required Humidity: and Temperature: labels remain required. Numeric comparisons allow 0.05 rounding tolerance.",
    "LCD metadata checks establish API configuration and printed field coordinates, not physical pixel correctness. Correct retained display content does not require repeated printing.",
    "Invalid sensor readings have no specified behavior and are not tested. The reference elects to retain the last valid display on invalid readings."
  ],
  "horizon_ms": 25000,
